'''three-quarter, three-quarters''' (thrē′kwâr′tėr, -tėrz), ''a.'' Involving anything three fourths of its normal size or proportions; specifically, noting a size of portraiture measuring 30 inches by 25, or a portrait delineated to the hips only.
